    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23062_english_2025-12-18.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-18-2025-12-18-0223",
    "chunk_index": 223,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c37f97acacefb02d881009981e2ba383",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1314,
    "chunk_text": "Also, I must mention, Sir, the commitment of our employees working abroad. They did fund collections from their own earnings. Some of them have collected money from their routine restaurants, businesses and also donated their salaries. What a commitment! That shows their affection and love for their own countrymates. So, I must mention here their commitment. They all have got together in this effort. That shows our resilience and their affection towards the country.\n\n3097 3098\n\n[\u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0dc3\u0dda \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dcf\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0db8:\u0dc3\u0dd0\u0dda\u0db6\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 08\n\nCommander? So, the Tri-forces have full confidence in the exemplary leadership that has been exhibited by him as a national leader. We must bow to him for his strategic direction.\n\nSir, I must also mention about the India-Pakistan involvement in this. Though, they have disparities or differences - they were not in good terms because they have fought many wars in the history - they have left aside all bad memories and have come together to save the people in Sri Lanka. We must appreciate India and Pakistan for their involvement and approach in this time of need.\n\nAlso, I must mention how foreign dignitaries appreciated our resilience, especially what the UN Resident Coordinator said about our resilience and togetherness."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
